# Scoped per-command sudo authorization for the demo/display tooling.
#
# The ONLY root surface granted NOPASSWD is the committed, reviewed deploy
# script below. The script itself whitelists its operations (mpv + chafa via
# apt-get); nothing outside it may escalate without a password. Never widen
# this to a bare binary or to /usr/bin/env or /bin/sh (that would be blanket
# root -- pyinfra's sh/env wrap is exactly why this boundary exists: it is
# a single authorized path, so the wrapper never matters).
#
# <REPO_USER> and <REPO_ROOT> are placeholders filled in by `just authorize`
# (this file is committed as a template because paths are machine-specific).
#
# Install:   just authorize          (runs as your user, prompts for sudo once)
# Verify:    sudo visudo -c
<REPO_USER> ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: <REPO_ROOT>/scripts/deploy_demo_tools.sh
